      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does not work against current Let\u0027s Encrypt acmev2 endpoint. On POST /new-acct for existing account boulder returns only URL in Location, no account data [0]. Therefore body decoding below fails with \"EOF\", and this error is propagated up to entry point.\n\nTo my understanding, acme draft [1] is ambiguous enough to allow both behaviours. Anyway, we need better error reporting here and a test for that.\n\nSuprisingly, GetAccount works, as doAccount only parses location.\n\nI believe integration test works because the url is already cached.\n\n[0] https://github.com/letsencrypt/boulder/blame/master/wfe2/wfe.go#L502\n[1] https://ietf-wg-acme.github.io/acme/draft-ietf-acme-acme.html#rfc.section.7.3.1",
